    "abstract": "We report for the first time the magnetic structure of the high entropy oxide (Mg0.2Co0.2Ni0.2Cu0.2Zn0.2)O using neutron powder diffraction. This material exhibits a sluggish magnetic transition but possesses a long-range ordered antiferromagnetic ground state, as revealed by DC and AC magnetic susceptibility, elastic and inelastic neutron scattering measurements. The magnetic propagation wavevector is k =(½, ½, ½) based on the cubic structure Fm - 3 m , and the magnetic structure consists of ferromagnetic sheets in the (111) planes with spins antiparallel between two neighboring planes. Inelastic neutron scattering reveals strong magnetic excitations at 100 K that survive up to room temperature. This work demonstrates that entropy-stabilized oxides represent a unique platform to study long range magnetic order with extreme chemical disorder.",
